{title: Jesus, Savior, Pilot Me}
{artist: Edward Hopper / John E. Gould}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: A}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 90}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Gospel Hymns Nos. 1 to 6 Complete, by Ira D. Sankey, James McGranahan & George C Stebbins (Chicago, Illinois: Biglow & Main, 1894), # 366)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Jesus, Savior, pilot me
[A]Over [D]life’s tem[E]pestuous [A]sea;
[E7]Unknown waves before me roll,__[A]__
[E7]Hiding rock and treacherous shoal.__[A]__
[A]Chart and compass come from Thee;
[A]Jesus, [D]Savior, [E]pilot [A]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]While th’apostles’ fragile bark
[A]Struggled [D]with the [E]billows [A]dark,
[E7]On the stormy Galilee,__[A]__
[E7]Thou didst walk upon the sea;__[A]__
[A]And when they beheld Thy form,
[A]Safe they [D]glided [E]through the [A]storm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Though the sea be smooth and bright,
[A]Sparkling [D]with the [E]stars of [A]night,
[E7]And my ship’s path be ablaze__[A]__
[E7]With the light of halcyon days,__[A]__
[A]Still I know my need of Thee;
[A]Jesus, [D]Savior, [E]pilot [A]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[A]When the darkling heavens frown,
[A]And the [D]wrathful [E]winds come [A]down,
[E7]And the fierce waves, tossed on high,__[A]__
[E7]Lash themselves against the sky,__[A]__
[A]Jesus, Savior, pilot me,
[A]Over [D]life’s tem[E]pestuous [A]sea.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[A]As a mother stills her child,
[A]Thou canst [D]hush the [E]ocean [A]wild;
[E7]Boisterous waves obey Thy will,__[A]__
[E7]When Thou sayest to them, Be still!__[A]__
[A]Wondrous sovereign of the sea,
[A]Jesus, [D]Savior, [E]pilot [A]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[A]When at last I near the shore,
[A]And the [D]fearful [E]breakers [A]roar
[E7]’Twixt me and the peaceful rest,__[A]__
[E7]Then, while leaning on Thy breast,__[A]__
[A]May I hear Thee say to me,
[A]Fear not, [D]I will [E]pilot [A]thee.
{end_of_verse}
